@GeographyNow and what laws apply where in native reservations are a clusterfuck and vary by state and reservation. At both federal and state levels. 

Especially in Public Law 280 states and the “compacts” they have with individual reservations. 

Still, US government has authority.

@KrishS-v9v9g It's all semantics. 
Internationally recognised borders of "China" _does_ include Taiwan, only one Chinese state is allowed to represent "China" internationally (right now that is the PRC) and you either represent all of it or don’t represent it at all, unlike Korea for instance, courtesy of the silly One China principle. 
On that note the ROC _does_ officially claim Taiwan to be part of China also, as an extension of them also still claiming the rest of China in their constitution. Obviously what's written on paper does not account for the context of what's actually happening IRL.
